[2026-09-14T11:46:09.486] Cog0  BD-NOTE,phase 2 starts a driver cog at commanded zero on P0_P15 then on P16_P31 and stops it; nothing is ever commanded to turn
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.487] Cog0  BD-NOTE,the gate on phase 2 is compile-time only -- there is no keypress and no runtime branch anywhere in this binary
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.489] Cog0  BD-NOTE,BD-GATE answer and BD-BUILD phase2_compiled carry the same fact from two places and MUST agree; a disagreement voids the run
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.490] Cog0  BD-NOTE,sweeping a group briefly drives its base+4 -- GUARD: a group whose base+4 lands on a declared board's pin other than that board's own base+4 is never swept
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.492] Cog0  BD-NOTE,GUARD: it is computed from the declared LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE in every sweep; on the bench bases that skips NO_USE_P24_P39 (P28 = RIGHT base+12) and P40_P55 (P44 = LEFT base+12)
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.494] Cog0  BD-NOTE,GUARD: a skipped cell emits one BD-SKIPPED record with its reason and no BD-REP; BD-SWEEP end counts cells and skipped and reps so cells plus skipped equals the plan
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.495] Cog0  BD-NOTE,-D DETECT_NO_TAIL drops P8_P23 and NO_USE_P24_P39 only; it is not a safety build because the guard runs in every build
