[2026-09-14T11:46:09.498] Cog0  BD-NOTE,VOID RULE: a log with no BD-BANNER or with cfg_id not equal to BENCH or with BD-CLK match 0 is VOID -- not suspect but void
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.499] Cog0  BD-NOTE,VOID RULE: any BD-ENUM match 0 voids the run -- the local pin-group table has drifted from the library's
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.500] Cog0  BD-NOTE,SUM RULE: sum 0 is real data on a Rev A board and is also what a loop that never executed produces
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.501] Cog0  BD-NOTE,SUM RULE: sum 0 is trustworthy ONLY when sumtix is at least 500 -- 500 Spin2 pinreads cannot complete in under 500 ticks
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.503] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CAL RULE: BD-CAL is emitted three times against a pin held driven high so the loop can never exit early
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.504] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CAL RULE: if the three tix_per_iter values differ by more than a few percent then every sumtix and every fltix in this log is void
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.506] Cog0  BD-NOTE,CROSS-CHECK: iter and (fltix / tix_per_iter) are two independent routes to the same number; if they disagree the instrumentation is lying
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.507] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: pre and post are each assembled from TWO 8-pin pinread calls (low half in bits 0-7 high half in bits 8-15)
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.508] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: that split is required because ADDPINS cannot cross a 32-pin port boundary; pre and post are therefore NOT atomic
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.509] Cog0  BD-NOTE,R1 NOTE: the lost atomicity is acceptable because pre and post are context snapshots and are not the measured interval
[2026-09-14T11:46:09.511] Cog0  BD-NOTE,HALL: bits 5 6 and 7 of a pre field are pin_hall_u/v/w so with a motor plugged in a valid 3-bit hall code is objective evidence the rail is powered
